{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/239545-initiation-of-pacts","id":239545,"title":"Initiation of Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-24T14:03:28-07:00","id":239545,"title":"Initiation of Pacts","content":"Once a Pact is made, when do its effects begin? Does a demon need to incorporate aspects of a Cover immediately, or can she hold them 'in storage' until she needs them? If the later, can she assemble them into a potential cover before attaching them to herself and taking up a Cover slot?<br /> <br /> And for that matter, if the Cover aspects can be held 'in storage', what happens to the elements they represent in the meantime? For example, say a demon Pacts for a mortal's pet as a Lesser Cover aspect. If the demon does not need to immediately incorporate the pet/owner relationship into an established Cover, does the pet 1). Still maintain the relationship with the mortal until the Pact is integrated into a Cover; 2). wander off, existing without an owner; or 3). Disappear, existing only as a (quantum) potential pet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T15:19:26-07:00","id":239608,"title":"","content":"The text doesn't really go into it. Closest I have to a hard answer is that you don't have to spend the XP you get in a pact immediately so it's safe to say that you don't have to commit it to a cover straight away. What happens while it isn't spent is not touched on. Later I might stop by with my suggestions since my houserules deal a lot with nailing down parts of the cover system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:11:21-07:00","id":239685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/239545-initiation-of-pacts?p=239608#post239608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text doesn't really go into it. Closest I have to a hard answer is that you don't have to spend the XP you get in a pact immediately so it's safe to say that you don't have to commit it to a cover straight away. What happens while it isn't spent is not touched on. Later I might stop by with my suggestions since my houserules deal a lot with nailing down parts of the cover system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you posted those anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:06:50-07:00","id":239974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/239545-initiation-of-pacts?p=239685#post239685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have you posted those anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as yet, no<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hRBzXtupWVyUYn3hRNa2YQiiKbBQs7O1o_ag9lMMeH4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> are my rough first drafts for cover-related houserules and expansions for my games. These are all theoretical, they haven't seen any actual play data yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 08-25-2014, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T23:50:32-08:00","id":301893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent, p. 192</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">These changes usually occur quickly and do so subtly enough that<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> they usually don\u2019t alert the God-Machine and its angels. However,<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> it is much easier for a demon to change a person, such as by making<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> an ugly man into a beautiful one, than it is to grant untold riches<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> or love, as this involves changing the world around them instead.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say most changes occur within a scene. Smaller changes are almost instant (unless it doesn't make much dramatic sense), while larger ones might take a little while, but no longer than a scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent, p. 116</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">It is possible to build a Cover whole-cloth using the small<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> pieces of other people\u2019s souls acquired through patch jobs. This<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> takes some time and the Cover thus created is usually extremely<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> fragile, but if the character can get it established, it is extremely<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> difficult to break. Demons that create patchwork Covers find<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">them to be the most rewarding and comfortable of all Covers \u2014<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> after all, they are custom made.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>System: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The demon simply spends Cover experiences<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> gained from patch jobs (see above) to build a new Cover. This<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> Cover can wind up being a little disjointed \u2014 the demon takes<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> a boyfriend from one person, a drug habit from another, and<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> a job as a ma\u00eetre d\u2019 from a third and has to make it all work<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> together cohesively \u2014 but once the Cover rating increases<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> to 5, the Cover solidifies considerably.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So, you don't have to spend Cover Experiences right away. I'd say in the meantime, the affected Cover aspect hovers in a state of uncertainty. In the example above, if you take someone's boyfriend but don't add it to a Cover right away, he is no longer dating the pact-signer but not dating the demon, either. In some cases, this might not make sense to the world (and draw attention), or might end up costing the demon if something happens to that would-be patch in the meantime.<br /> <br /> Signing for ownership of a company but not actually adding it to your Cover might cause the company to crash in the meantime. At least, that's one idea. I'd certainly allow for other interpretations, like a strange sort of stasis in an entropic world. The company's stocks don't rise or fall, it makes no profit but spends no money, etc., basically existing in a state of Schrodinger's uncertainty until some other force acts upon it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}